  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The ranking lists the largest federal contracts by total value in FY2027 to date. NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC holds the top spot at $44.1B. UT-BATTELLE LLC follows at $43B. LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC is third at $42.2B. TRIAD NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC is fourth at $36.3B. CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC is fifth at $35.2B. BATTELLE MEMORIAL INSTITUTE is sixth at $31.2B. SAVANNAH RIVER NUCLEAR SOLUTIONS LLC is seventh at $28B. BATTELLE ENERGY ALLIANCE, LLC is eighth at $26.8B. THE BOEING COMPANY is ninth at $22.7B. THE REGENTS OF THE UNIVERSITY OF CALIFORNIA is tenth at $20.2B. Total obligations are $44.1B. The note clarifies that total award value figures are full contract values, not single-year obligations, so rankings reflect full contract amounts rather than annual funding levels.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which contractors top the FY2027 list?",
        "body": "NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC leads the list at $44.1B. UT-BATTELLE LLC and LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC are close behind at $43B and $42.2B respectively. TRIAD NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC and CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC round out the top five at $36.3B and $35.2B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What types of organizations appear among the largest contracts?",
        "body": "National laboratory management entities dominate the top of the list, including UT-BATTELLE LLC, LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC, and THE REGENTS OF THE UNIVERSITY OF CALIFORNIA. Defense and energy integrators also appear, including THE BOEING COMPANY at $22.7B and BATTELLE MEMORIAL INSTITUTE at $31.2B."
      }
    ]
  },
